      "id": "54099a76-0db0-4dc2-addb-f1ce1a24a883",
      "name": "Sticky Note2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. AI Analysis & Classification Engine\n\nThe connected LLM analyzes incoming client IT support issues and determines the main category, subcategory, priority, severity, appropriate support team and support level and outputs them as a structured JSON.",
        "height": 288,
        "width": 288,
        "color": "#0C4BE9"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1360,
        -384
      ],
      "id": "2e8b885f-0ec2-40b6-a98b-1f53ecf38843",
      "name": "Sticky Note3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze the following IT support request:\n\nClient Name:\n{{ $json.name }}\n\nIssue Title:\n{{ $json.subject }}\n\nIssue Description:\n{{ $json.issue }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "needsFallback": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are an IT support ticket classification assistant.  Your task is to analyze incoming IT support issues and classify them for an automated ticket management system.  Analyze the client's issue and determine:  1. The main category of the issue. 2. The specific subcategory. 3. The priority level. 4. The severity level. 5. The client's sentiment. 6. A concise summary of the issue. 7. The most appropriate support team. 8. The recommended support level.  Priority levels: - Critical: Major outage or issue affecting multiple users or critical business operations. - High: Serious issue preventing an individual user or important business function from working. - Medium: Issue affecting productivity but with a possible workaround. - Low: Minor issue, general request, or issue that does not significantly affect operations.  Severity levels: - Critical - High - Medium - Low  Possible support teams include: - Network Support - Hardware Support - Software Support - Security Team - Email Support - General IT Support  Support levels: - Level 1 Support - Level 2 Support - Level 3 Support  Do not invent information that is not present in the client's request.  Return your analysis in the required structured format. Possible categories include:- Email - Network - Software - Hardware"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1392,
        -80
      ],
      "id": "9d9cbbed-1212-49fd-81b5-ff02ea727227",
      "name": "Analysis & Classification",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Priority to SLA Converter\n\nBased on the priority obtained from the LLM, this node determines how quickly the issue must be handled.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 208,
        "color": "#0C4BE9"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1680,
        -336
      ],
      "id": "8dad6e31-23d5-4bab-b4b4-cd10cfc5824e",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const priority =\n  ($json.output.priority || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n\nconst slaHours = {\n  critical: 1,\n  high: 4,\n  medium: 8,\n  low: 24\n};\n\nconst hours = slaHours[priority] ?? 24;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...$json,\n    sla_hours: hours,\n    sla_assigned_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    sla_deadline: new Date(\n      Date.now() + hours * 60 * 60 * 1000\n    ).toISOString()\n  }\n};"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1744,
        -80
      ],
      "id": "ac485f57-deeb-45bf-b2b0-ddff1339b391",
      "name": "SLA Calculator"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. Ticketer\n\nCreates the actual ticket in Airtable using relevant client information obtained from previous nodes. Automatically assigns a ticket number for every new record and sets the ticket status as \"Open\".",
        "height": 288,
        "color": "#0C4BE9"
      },
